# Complexity

Let:

```text
m = length of nums1
n = length of nums2
```

We perform binary search only on the smaller array.

### Time Complexity

```text
O(log(min(m, n)))
```

This satisfies the required:

```text
O(log(m + n))
```

### Space Complexity

```text
O(1)
```

No additional array is created.

---

# Key Takeaway

The important trick is:

> **Do not merge the two sorted arrays. Find the correct partition using Binary Search.**

```text
Two Sorted Arrays
       ↓
Choose Smaller Array
       ↓
Binary Search Partition
       ↓
Check Partition
       ↓
Find Middle Values
       ↓
Calculate Median
```

This reduces the time from **O(m + n)** to **O(log(min(m, n)))**.
